<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emil Hácha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emil Hácha was a Czech lawyer who became President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a> in 1938. Summoned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in March 1939, he was pressured into accepting German occupation, and he served as state president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> under German control. Arrested after the war, he died in prison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emil-hacha.jpg" alt="Emil Hácha" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emil_H%C3%A1cha_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
